<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  /* Basic styling to mimic document structure */
  body { font-family: "Liberation Serif", "DejaVu Serif", Georgia, serif; }
  h1, h2 { font-weight: bold; }
  .header-info { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section { margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .signature-block { margin-top: 50px; }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <img src="" alt="Ohio Department of Taxation Logo" style="height: 40px;">
      <p>Department of Taxation</p>
      <p><span data-field="tax_website_url">{{ tax_website_url }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>STEC B</p>
      <p>Rev. 3/15</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h1>Sales and Use Tax</h1>
    <h2>Blanket Exemption Certificate</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>The purchaser hereby claims exemption or exemption on all purchases of tangible personal property and selected services made under this certificate from:</p>
    <p><span data-field="certificate_reference_number">{{ certificate_reference_number }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>(Vendor's name)</p>
    <p><span data-field="vendor_name">{{ vendor_name }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>and certifies that the claim is based upon the purchaser's proposed use of the items or services, the activity of the purchase, or both, as shown herein:</p>
    <p>This sale is exempt under Ohio law, pursuant to Ohio Revised Code Section 5739.02(B)(1), as a sale to the State of Ohio or any of its political subdivisions. Purchases of the Telecommunication Services are exempt as defined by Ohio Revised Code Section 5739.01(B)(3)(F) and 5739.01(AA).</p>
    <p>This certificate shall continue in force until revoked. It shall be considered a part of each order given the above-named vendor unless otherwise specified.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3>Purchaser must state a valid reason for claiming exemption or exemption.</h3>
    <p><strong>Purchaser's Name:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.name">{{ purchaser.name }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Higher Education:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.higher_education_status">{{ purchaser.higher_education_status }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Purchaser's type of business:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.business_type">{{ purchaser.business_type }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Street address:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.address.street">{{ purchaser.address.street }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>City, state, ZIP code:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.address.city_state_zip">{{ purchaser.address.city_state_zip }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Signature:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.signature_name">{{ purchaser.signature_name }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Title:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.title">{{ purchaser.title }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Date signed:</strong> <span data-field="purchaser.date_signed">{{ purchaser.date_signed }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Vendor's license number, if any:</strong> <span data-field="vendor.license_number">{{ vendor.license_number }}</span></p>
    <p><strong>Federal Tax ID Number:</strong> <span data-field="vendor.tax_id">{{ vendor.tax_id }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>Vendors of motor vehicles, titled watercraft and titled outboard motors may use this certificate to purchase these items under the "resale" exception. Otherwise, purchaser must comply with either rule 5703-9-10 or 5703-9-25 of the Administrative Code. This certificate cannot be used by construction contractors to purchase material for incorporation into real property under an exempt construction contract. Construction contractors must comply with rule 5703-9-14 of the Administrative Code.</p>
  </div>
</div>